  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I found no past ticket that reports this exact problem. Your log shows an IOException because WinGet\\\\KeyboardShortcuts\\\\+WindowsNT.Notepad.en-US.yml was locked by another process while the bundled manifests were being copied. No archived ticket mentions that. The related tickets are different. #48170 is a missing Manifests directory on launch. #48448 and #48522 are crashes when switching sections in 0.100.0. #48638 is an access violation crash. Please file this as a new bug in the Shortcut Guide area and include the log snippet and your version, 0.100.2. As a possible workaround, which I have not confirmed, close any program that may be holding the Notepad manifest file open, such as Notepad or a sync or antivirus tool. Then restart PowerToys and try Shortcut Guide again.\"}",
